<title>SAUDI ARABIA: Saudi SCECO in $23.5 mln deal with Marubeni.</title>
<headline>Saudi SCECO in $23.5 mln deal with Marubeni.</headline>
<dateline>DAMMAM, Saudi Arabia 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Consolidated Electric Company - East (SCECO-East) on Tuesday awarded an 88 million riyal ($23.5 million) contract to Marubeni Saudi Arabia Company Limited, a subsidiary of Japan's Marubeni Corp, for the expansion of a substation.</p>
<p>The project, which is due to be completed in 1999, was one of four deals worth 1.159 billion riyals ($309 million) awarded by SCECO-East to integrate its new power plant into the main generating system to keep pace with domestic demand. ($=3.75 riyals)</p>
</text>
